h(2, id: "diagrams") { 11.5 Diagrams, charts, and graphs }

p {
    A mermaid block is a diagram source. A chart block and a graph block are
    tables of numbers, and the compiler draws them as SVG in the HTML file.
}

h(3, id: "mermaid") { 11.5.1 mermaid }

p {
    The body is a raw scope, same as code{math}. Optional code{caption} is a
    string. The page loads Mermaid only when a document has one of these blocks.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
mermaid(caption: "Build flow") {!
flowchart LR
  A[Parse] --> B[Format]
  B --> C[HTML]
\!}
!}

p { An empty body is a semantic error. }

h(3, id: "chart") { 11.5.2 chart }

p {
    code{chart} defaults to code{type: "bar"}. code{graph} defaults to
    code{type: "line"}. Both also accept code{pie}. Optional code{title} is the
    figure title.
}

p {
    The body is rows, same as a table. The first cell is the label. Later cells
    are numbers. A header row names the series. Every row must have the same
    number of cells, and a pie chart cannot use a negative or all-zero column.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
chart(type: "bar", title: "Passes") {
  row(header: true) {
    cell { Step }
    cell { Count }
  }
  row { cell { parse } cell { 3 } }
  row { cell { fmt } cell { 9 } }
}

graph(title: "Time") {
  row(header: true) {
    cell { Step }
    cell { ms }
  }
  row { cell { lex } cell { 4 } }
  row { cell { parse } cell { 6 } }
}

chart(type: "pie", title: "Share") {
  row { cell { docs } cell { 5 } }
  row { cell { tests } cell { 3 } }
}
!}

p { The same blocks, drawn on this page: }

mermaid(caption: "Build flow") {!
flowchart LR
  A[Parse] --> B[Format]
  B --> C[HTML]
!}

chart(title: "Passes") {
    row(header: true) {
        cell { Step }
        cell { Before }
        cell { After }
    }
    row {
        cell { parse }
        cell { 3 }
        cell { 8 }
    }
    row {
        cell { fmt }
        cell { 1 }
        cell { 9 }
    }
}

graph(title: "Time") {
    row(header: true) {
        cell { Step }
        cell { ms }
    }
    row {
        cell { lex }
        cell { 4 }
    }
    row {
        cell { parse }
        cell { 6 }
    }
    row {
        cell { gen }
        cell { 5 }
    }
}

chart(type: "pie", title: "Share") {
    row {
        cell { docs }
        cell { 5 }
    }
    row {
        cell { samples }
        cell { 2 }
    }
    row {
        cell { tests }
        cell { 3 }
    }
}
